# Vercel -> your project -> Settings -> Environment Variables (Production and Preview).
#
# ONLY add the variables listed in this file. Do NOT paste your local .env.local into Vercel:
# it contains localhost addresses (and a test password) that must never reach a deployed site.
#
# Live updates connect straight to the API host (Vercel cannot proxy websockets). The app works without this; it just won't update live.
VITE_SOCKET_URL=https://b2b-project-v91w.onrender.com

# Do NOT set VITE_API_BASE_URL: in production the app calls same-origin /api, which frontend/vercel.json proxies to Render.
# Do NOT set VITE_TEST_PASSWORD, and never put secrets in VITE_* variables: they are bundled into the public JavaScript.
#
# Variables only apply to NEW deployments. After changing them, redeploy (Deployments -> ... -> Redeploy, untick "use existing build cache").
